  </para>
  <para>Notice that, in the case when \(m\) and \(n\) have opposite signs, the sign of the one with the larger absolute
    value matches the sign of \(b\).</para>
  
</note>

<title>Try It: How to Factor a Trinomial of the Form \(x^2 + bx + c\)</title>
<para>Factor each trinomial.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(
    q^2 + 10q + 24\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(−7n + 12 + n^2\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(m^2 − 13mn + 12n^2\) </item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
<title>Solution</title>
<para>Check your solutions for factoring trinomials of the form \(x^2 + bx + c\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(
    (q + 4)(q + 6)\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((n − 3)(n − 4)\) </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((m − n)(m − 12n)\) </item>
</list>
</section>
